# Comparable research conventions

When creating or editing comparable research, FINDINGS, screenshot paths, or capture scripts, follow these so the workflow stays repeatable.

## Folder and paths

- One folder per company: `docs/research/comparables/[company-slug]/`.
- Each company has `FINDINGS.md` and optionally `screenshots/[YYYY-MM-DD]/[url-path-slug].png`.
- **URL path → file slug**: `/` → `landing`; `/pricing` → `pricing`; `/blog/post-name` → `blog-post-name`. Use lowercase, hyphens for path segments, no leading/trailing hyphens.

## FINDINGS.md structure

Use `docs/research-templates/COMPARABLE_RESEARCH_TEMPLATE.md`. Sections:

1. URL (primary + other)
2. Docs last updated
3. Docs created
4. Value props (bullets)
5. Customer complaints / issues
6. What this company is NOT solving
7. **Screenshots (all key URLs)** — table: Date | URL / path | File (link to `screenshots/[date]/[slug].png`)
8. Citations / references
9. Notes
10. Changelog

When adding or updating section 7, use the table format; link files under `screenshots/[YYYY-MM-DD]/`.

## Screenshot discovery

- Prefer same-origin links from the landing page; optionally URLs from `/sitemap.xml`.
- Skip `/api`, sitemap.xml, and binary extensions (.pdf, .zip, etc.).
- Cap number of URLs per site to avoid timeouts (e.g. 25 from page, 30 from sitemap).

## Capture script (scripts/capture-all-comparables.js)

- Company list: `COMPANIES` array with `{ slug, primaryUrl }`.
- New company: add entry to `COMPANIES` and create `docs/research/comparables/[slug]/FINDINGS.md` from template.
- Subset run: `COMPANIES=slug1,slug2 node scripts/capture-all-comparables.js [date]`.
- Script writes screenshots to `[company-slug]/screenshots/[date]/[slug].png` and updates section 7 in each FINDINGS.md.

## TLDR

- Keep `docs/research/TLDR_RESEARCH.md` with 1–2 positioning bullets per company; update when adding or refreshing comparables.
